@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# Verify a manually-published post — CON-153.
# POST /api/posts/:id/verify-external confirms a post that was published
# by hand ON the platform (outside Ogen) exists, using Zernio's on-demand
# sync-external (POST /posts/sync-external). On a match it:
#   - resolves the post's connected Zernio account (CON-150 rules),
#   - back-fills posts.publisher_post_id + marks the post `published`,
#   - writes a first analytics snapshot (so GET /api/posts/:id/analytics
#     starts returning it — see analytics/analytics.http), and
#   - emits post.analytics.updated on the SSE stream.
# It's the fast path to start tracking a manual post's analytics instead of
# waiting ~90 min for the background external sync.
#
# Body — at least one locator:
#   { "url": "https://..." }         any format the platform uses
#   { "post_id": "platform-media-id" }
#
# Responses:
#   200 { found: true, post: { id, publisher_post_id, sync_status: "synced" },
#         analytics: { impressions, reach, likes, comments, shares, saves,
#                      clicks, views, engagement_rate } }
#   200 { found: false }                 platform has no such post (upstream 404)
#   400 url or post_id required          empty body
#   404 post not found                   unknown Ogen post id
#   409 { error: "no_account_connected", platform }   no account for the platform
#   422 { error: "account_selection_required", platform, candidates: [...] }
#         2+ same-platform accounts and the post carries no social_account_id
#   502                                  sync-external upstream failure
#   503                                  Zernio not configured / no profile
#
# All endpoints require authentication. Run "Login" from sessions/sessions.http
# first — the HTTP client stores and replays the cookie automatically.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - {{campaignId}} set (run campaigns/campaigns.http → createCampaign).
#   - At least one Zernio account connected for the post's platform (run the
#     connect flow in publishers/zernio/zernio.http). With exactly ONE account
#     the endpoint auto-selects it; with two or more and no explicit
#     social_account_id on the post it returns 422 account_selection_required.

@linkedinPlatformId = AXqWG7U2qnpt

###
# ── Setup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###

### Helper — create a LinkedIn post published manually on the platform  [protected]
# @name createManualPost
# A plain draft stands in for "created in Ogen but published by hand": it has a
# platform but no publisher_post_id yet — exactly what verify-external back-fills.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "campaign_id": "{{campaignId}}",
  "platform_id": "{{linkedinPlatformId}}",
  "platform_post_type": "article",
  "title": "Published by hand on LinkedIn",
  "content": "This post was published manually on the platform, outside Ogen.",
  "status": "draft",
  "cta_type": "none"
}

> {% client.global.set("manualPostId", response.body.id) %}

###
# ── Verify scenarios ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###

### 1. Verify by URL — matched → 200 found  [protected]
# Paste the URL the user copied after publishing on the platform.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{manualPostId}}/verify-external
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:1234567890"
}

### 2. Verify by platform post id — alternative locator  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{manualPostId}}/verify-external
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "post_id": "urn:li:activity:1234567890"
}

### 3. Not found on the platform → 200 { found: false }  [protected]
# A URL/id the account's recent posts don't include.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{manualPostId}}/verify-external
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:0000000000"
}

### 4. Neither url nor post_id → 400  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{manualPostId}}/verify-external
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 5. Unknown Ogen post id → 404  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/nonexistent/verify-external
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:1234567890"
}

### 6. Confirm the back-fill — the snapshot is now readable  [protected]
# After scenario 1 succeeds, the per-post analytics endpoint returns the
# freshly-written snapshot instead of 409/pending (see analytics/analytics.http).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{manualPostId}}/analytics
Accept: application/json
